### Variables
@baseUrl = https://localhost:5285
@tenantId = root
@adminEmail = admin@root.com
@adminPassword = P@ssw0rd
@targetUserId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 1. Login as Admin
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/tokens
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant: {{tenantId}}

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

### Extract admin token
@adminToken = {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 2. Get list of users (to find a user to impersonate)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/users?pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
X-Tenant: {{tenantId}}

### 3. Impersonate a user
# @name impersonate
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/impersonate
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
X-Tenant: {{tenantId}}

{
  "userId": "{{targetUserId}}"
}

### Extract impersonation token
@impersonationToken = {{impersonate.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 4. Make requests as impersonated user
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/me
Authorization: Bearer {{impersonationToken}}
X-Tenant: {{tenantId}}

### 5. Get user permissions (should be target user's permissions)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/users/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{impersonationToken}}
X-Tenant: {{tenantId}}

### 6. Stop impersonation
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/impersonate/stop
Authorization: Bearer {{impersonationToken}}
X-Tenant: {{tenantId}}

### 7. Try to use impersonation token after stopping (should fail or show warning)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/me
Authorization: Bearer {{impersonationToken}}
X-Tenant: {{tenantId}}

### 8. Login again as admin to get fresh token
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/tokens
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant: {{tenantId}}

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}
